        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Determine the pH of a 0.055-M HCl solution."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "bhjmhmxquf54vxq",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Because HCl is a strong acid, every molecule of HCl in solution will dissociate into H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and Cl"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". Therefore, [H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] = [HCl] = 0.055 M."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "hnhgqci7gzhx72e",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Knowing the [H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "], the pH can be calculated:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "o0rk8kngk5b56pz",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "ziz91etp4jpmf11",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "mhmsi7sbmn45ds3",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm{pH}=-\\log\\lbrack{\\mathrm H}_3\\mathrm O^+\\rbrack=-\\log(0.055)=1.26",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The pH of 1.26 is very low, as would be expected for a strong acid."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "9uuceh1eea20ndv",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "id": "4125456267",
            "selection": {
              "anchor": {
                "offset": 0,
                "path": [
                  0,
                  0
                ]
              },
              "focus": {
                "offset": 0,
                "path": [
                  1,
                  0
                ]
              }
            },
            "type": "content"
          }
        ],
        "id": "3287043593",
        "layout": "vertical",
        "purpose": "example",
        "type": "group"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "A solution of Ca(OH)"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " has a concentration of 0.042 M. What is the pH of the solution?"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "9qml17uxsl362bv",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Because this is a strong base, it fully dissociates into its ions. For every one formula unit of Ca(OH)"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " present, one Ca"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "2+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ion and two OH"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ions are in the solution. Therefore, [OH"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] = 2(0.042 M) = 0.084 M."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "t75w8i4th13076l",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Knowing the [OH"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "], the pH can be calculated:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "v164pl6so705pcv",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "jugse1kad6lacak",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "46bxh0pniplho7m",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm{pOH}=-\\log\\lbrack\\mathrm{OH}^-\\rbrack=-\\log(0.084)=1.08",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "c72ihcnsskgef1e",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "rro8vkb3h22sma6",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm{pH}=14.00-\\mathrm{pOH}=14.00-1.08=12.92",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The pH of 12.92 is very low, as would be expected for a strong base."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "nkhwk482eg1gru6",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "id": "4206579195",
